# Olivia Rodrigo Drops Official Version of Melancholy ‘Miss This Christmas’ on Amazon Music

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from Rolling Stone Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Olivia Rodrigo has been letting the holiday spirit guide her lately: Just weeks after releasing her first Christmas song, “Take Me Home (4 Christmas),” she debuted the song’s B-side “Miss This Christmas” live in Nashville. Now, she’s dropping the official version of the track exclusively on Amazon Music .

Like her album you seem pretty sad for a girl so in love , the two holiday songs capture different sides of love and romance: “Take Me Home (4 Christmas)” is an upbeat, enthusiastic track, inspired by Christmas songs from the Eighties as Rodrigo sings about the anticipation of meeting a significant other’s family. A playful video starred SNL cast member Ben Marshall as the guy bringing her home for Christmas, while Cynthia Nixon took on the role of Marshall’s mom meeting Rodrigo for the first time.

Earlier this month, she performed “Take Me Home (4 Christmas) (Songline Version),” recorded at the Brooklyn Botanic Garden in New York City and directed by Bradley J. Calder. That performance is also streaming exclusively on Amazon Music and available on YouTube .

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

Rodrigo was one of the artists with the most Grammy nominations this year: She scored seven nods for you seem pretty sad for a girl so in love , including Album of the Year, Song of the Year, and Record of the Year. Her Unraveled tour will run through Dec. 20 in Las Vegas, and then pick up with a residency in Los Angeles from Jan. 12 through 29.

